# Do not touch — protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts`
(`AppState`, `Task`, `Action` union, `initialState`) are load-bearing: every
other module depends on their shape. Silent edits there ripple through the
whole app and are the most expensive mistakes an agent can make here.

## Rule

- Treat these paths as PROTECTED:
  - `app/src/store.ts`
  - `app/src/types.ts`
  - `app/package.json`, `app/tsconfig.json`
- NEVER edit a protected file without explicit approval in the current
  conversation. If a task seems to require it, STOP and ask first, showing the
  exact proposed diff and why `reducer.ts`/`actions.ts` are not enough.
  If asking is impossible (non-interactive run), choose the least invasive
  additive option — e.g. an OPTIONAL field (`priority?: Priority`) so existing
  code and test fixtures keep compiling — and flag it in the final report.
- Keep the diff of a protected file MINIMAL: add lines only. NEVER reformat,
  re-align or reorder existing declarations (e.g. column-aligning the `Action`
  union) while adding a variant.
- The ONLY routinely allowed change to `types.ts` is ADDING a new variant to
  the `Action` union (or adding an optional field to an existing interface) —
  and only when the user asked for that feature. Never change or remove
  existing fields/signatures.
- NEVER change the public signatures of `createStore`, the existing action
  creators, or `app/src/lib/text.ts` functions — extend, do not rewrite.
- Feature work belongs in `reducer.ts`, `actions.ts`, `selectors.ts`,
  `lib/`, and colocated tests.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --name-only` → `app/src/store.ts` does not appear unless the user
   explicitly approved it in this session.
2. `git diff app/src/types.ts` → shows only additive lines (a new `Action`
   variant / optional field); no removed or renamed existing members, and
   `git diff --numstat app/src/types.ts` shows `0` deletions.
3. `git diff app/package.json` → empty unless approved.
4. `cd app && npm test` → all pre-existing tests still pass unchanged.

